{"name":"Ultra Violet","hex":"#7366bd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ultra","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extreme; far beyond the norm; fanatical; uncompromising."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A political extremist, in particular.","An especially devoted football fan, typically organized and participating in choreographies (including pyrotechnics), often of outwardly intimidating demeanour, but distinguished from a violent hooligan (although overlap between both subcultures is possible)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ultra"},{"term":"violet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant or flower of the genus Viola, especially the fragrant Viola odorata;  similar-looking plants and flowers.","A person thought to resemble V. odorata, especially in its beauty and delicacy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a violet colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/violet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ultra Violet (Bananarama album)","blocks":[{"text":"Ultra Violet is the seventh studio album released by the English group Bananarama. Originally released under the title of I Found Love on 21 August 1995 only in Japan, the album was renamed as Ultra Violet and released on 2 February 1996 in Australia and some markets in Europe, such as Portugal and Spain. At the time of the original release, the album wasn't sold in the UK, the group's home market. Ultra Violet was eventually released in the United Kingdom on 7 August 2020. This also marked the first time the album was made available on vinyl as it was previously only available on compact disc and cassette."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Banana_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultra_Violet_(Bananarama_album)","wikidata":"Q4003258"},{"title":"Ultraviolet","blocks":[{"text":"Ultraviolet radiation is electromagnetic radiation of wavelengths of 100–400 nanometers, shorter than that of visible light, but longer than vacuum ultraviolet and extreme ultraviolet, radiation bands that overlaps UV but shares some properties with soft X-rays. UV radiation is present in sunlight and constitutes about 10% of the total electromagnetic radiation output from the Sun. It is also produced by electric arcs, Cherenkov radiation, and specialized lights, such as mercury-vapor lamps, tanning lamps, and black lights."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Pipefitter_welder_kutzo.jpg/330px-Pipefitter_welder_kutzo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ultraviolet","wikidata":"Q11391"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/82/Banana_uv.jpg/250px-Banana_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/82/Banana_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/8/82/Banana_uv.jpg/250px-Banana_uv.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABanana_uv.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/22/Banana_ifla.jpg/250px-Banana_ifla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/22/Banana_ifla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/22/Banana_ifla.jpg/250px-Banana_ifla.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABanana_ifla.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/UV-handlamp_hg.jpg/500px-UV-handlamp_hg.jpg?utm_source